<< /AP << /N 1072 0 R >> /C [ 1.0 0.819611 0.0 ] /CA 0.399994 /Contents <> /CreationDate (D:20260826172816+02'00') /F 4 /M (D:20260914175543+02'00') /NM (a285bed9-2f25-4687-9fc2-77f730c39c0e) /P 34 0 R /Popup 1073 0 R /QuadPoints [ 289.19 233.773 292.19 233.773 289.19 218.353 292.19 218.353 ] /RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.2pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">This should be substantiated by references. To my knowledge this typological division has been introduced by Jakobson and has been further developed by Isa&#269;enko. &#13;&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Isa&#269;enko, Aleksandr V. 1939&#8211;1940. Versuch einer Typologie der slavischen Sprachen.&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic">Linguistica Slovaca </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">I&#8211;II.64&#8211;76.</span></p></body>) /Rect [ 288.708 217.871 292.672 234.255 ] /Subj (Hervorheben) /Subtype /Highlight /T (Anonymous) /Type /Annot >>
