437 0 obj
<< /AP << /N 1134 0 R >> /C [ 1.0 0.819611 0.0 ] /CA 0.399994 /Contents (The use of these characters for the notation of Common Slavic forms is very unusual. I strongly recommend following one of the existing conventions. Other than that the proposed phoneme system is not original. So, I would abstain from calling it "my LCS".) /CreationDate (D:20260826225544+02'00') /F 4 /M (D:20260914175826+02'00') /NM (e5822809-8b9f-46ec-9da1-688de128c399) /P 36 0 R /Popup 1135 0 R /QuadPoints [ 395.55 642.961 403.482 642.961 395.55 624.169 403.482 624.169 424.074 642.961 431.598 642.961 424.074 624.169 431.598 624.169 ] /RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.6pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">The use of these characters for the notation of Common Slavic forms is very unusual. I strongly recommend following one of the existing conventions. Other than that the proposed phoneme system is not original. So, I would abstain from calling it &quot;my LCS&quot;.</span></p></body>) /Rect [ 394.963 623.582 432.185 643.548 ] /Subj (Hervorheben) /Subtype /Highlight /T (Anonymous) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
