459 0 obj
<< /AP << /N 1167 0 R >> /C [ 0.588242 0.262741 0.988235 ] /CA 0.399994 /Contents (Below the authors, in my opinion, correctly differenticate between palatal and secondarily palatized consonants. Please note that a palatal rhotic seems impossible to articulate which is why you should rather mark this consonant with a different diacritic \(as they do with other consonants below\). For the impossibility to articulate palatal rhotics see Stadnik \(2002 with references\) and recently Kavitskaya & Wandl \(2025\).\r\rStadnik, E. \(2002\): Die Palatalisierung in den Sprachen Europas und Asiens. Eine areal-typologische Untersuchung, Tübingen.\r\rDarya Kavitskaya & Florian Wandl. 2025. Preservation and loss of a rare contrast: Palatalization\rof rhotics in Slavic. In Natalia Kuznetsova, Cormac Anderson & Shelece Easterday \(eds.\), Rarities\rin phonetics and phonology: Structural, typological, evolutionary, and social dimensions, 575\205601.\rBerlin: Language Science Press. DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.15148188) /CreationDate (D:20260906221923+02'00') /F 4 /IT /HighlightNote /M (D:20260914175835+02'00') /NM (930c52c9-c138-4f47-99f2-610b38af4c07) /P 36 0 R /Popup 1168 0 R /QuadPoints [ 410.8 556.761 416.332 556.761 410.8 537.969 416.332 537.969 ] /RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Below the authors, in my opinion, correctly differenticate between palatal and secondarily palatized consonants. Please note that a palatal rhotic seems impossible to articulate which is why you should rather mark this consonant with a different diacritic \(as they do with other consonants below\). For the impossibility to articulate palatal rhotics see Stadnik \(2002 with references\) and recently Kavitskaya &amp; Wandl \(2025\).&#13;&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-16.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Stadnik, E. \(2002\): Die Palatalisierung in den Sprachen Europas und Asiens. Eine areal-typologische Untersuchung, T&#252;bingen.&#13;&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Darya Kavitskaya &amp; Florian Wandl. 2025. Preservation and loss of a rare contrast: Palatalization&#13;of rhotics in Slavic. In Natalia Kuznetsova, Cormac Anderson &amp; Shelece Easterday \(eds.\), </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic">Rarities&#13;in phonetics and phonology: Structural, typological, evolutionary, and social dimensions</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">, 575&#8211;601.&#13;Berlin: Language Science Press. </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#8A8A8A;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.15148188</span></p></body>) /Rect [ 410.213 537.382 416.919 557.348 ] /Subj (Kommentar zu Text) /Subtype /Highlight /T (Anonymous) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
