<< /AP << /N 1249 0 R >> /C [ 0.588242 0.262741 0.988235 ] /CA 0.399994 /Contents (As stated above, this is very idiosyncratic. Also, even though the dialectal pronouncation of the consonants written with these letters in BCMS is indeed that of palatal plosives, the letters are rather associated with palatal fricatives \(i.e. the pronunciation in standard Croatian\).) /CreationDate (D:20260906173345+02'00') /F 4 /IT /HighlightNote /M (D:20260914180233+02'00') /NM (6feeae37-fdd9-4c63-9cac-73e17c1929a2) /P 39 0 R /Popup 1250 0 R /QuadPoints [ 254.582 633.823 302.966 633.823 254.582 618.403 302.966 618.403 ] /RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">As stated above, this is very idiosyncratic. Also, even though the dialectal pronouncation of the consonants written with these letters in BCMS is indeed that of palatal plosives, the letters are rather associated with palatal fricatives \(i.e. the pronunciation in standard Croatian\).</span></p></body>) /Rect [ 254.1 617.921 303.448 634.305 ] /Subj (Kommentar zu Text) /Subtype /Highlight /T (Anonymous) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
