<< /AP << /N 1334 0 R >> /C [ 0.588242 0.262741 0.988235 ] /CA 0.399994 /Contents (It will not be clear to every reader why this is called compensatory lengthening. Moreover, there is an alternative opinion on this change which does not involve compensatory lengthening notably advocated for by Shevelov \(1979\).\r\rShevelov, G. \(1979\): A Historical Phonology of the Ukrainian Language, Heidelberg.) /CreationDate (D:20260906211900+02'00') /F 4 /IT /HighlightNote /M (D:20260914180610+02'00') /NM (78322299-9ea5-4607-9a23-8740fc1780b4) /P 42 0 R /Popup 1335 0 R /QuadPoints [ 109.384 521.703 56.8 521.703 109.384 537.123 56.8 537.123 499.561 535.503 421.633 535.503 499.561 550.923 421.633 550.923 ] /RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">It will not be clear to every reader why this is called compensatory lengthening. Moreover, there is an alternative opinion on this change which does not involve compensatory lengthening notably advocated for by Shevelov \(1979\).&#13;&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-16.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Shevelov, G. \(1979\): A Historical Phonology of the Ukrainian Language, Heidelberg.</span></p></body>) /Rect [ 56.3181 521.221 500.043 551.405 ] /Subj (Kommentar zu Text) /Subtype /Highlight /T (Anonymous) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
