1096 0 obj
<< /AP << /N 1573 0 R >> /C [ 1.0 0.819611 0.0 ] /CA 0.399994 /Contents (The authors are not very precise in their use of the term Common Slavic \(= Proto-Slavic?\), but the reconstruction of Proto-Slavic has changed significantly in the last years with the most vocal advocate for a more acurate reconstruction being Georg Holzer \(starting with Holzer 1995\). A good summary is given by Majer \(2020\). Calling this matter trivial is unexpected in a study which gives as one of its main objectives providing a tool for studying phonology.\r\rHolzer, Georg. 1995. Einheitlichkeit des Slavischen um 600 n. Chr. und ihr Zerfall. Wiener\rslavistisches Jahrbuch 41.55\20589.\r\rMajer, Marek \(2020\). Proto-Slavic. In Marc L. Greenberg \(ed.\), Encyclopedia of Slavic Languages and Linguistics Online. Brill. https://doi.org/10.1163/2589-6229_ESLO_COM_032015) /CreationDate (D:20260826185241+02'00') /F 4 /M (D:20260914175656+02'00') /NM (149ff413-5231-434e-8914-494775ad918c) /P 35 0 R /Popup 1095 0 R /QuadPoints [ 253.251 606.373 430.033 606.373 253.251 590.953 430.033 590.953 ] /RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.6pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">The authors are not very precise in their use of the term Common Slavic \(= Proto-Slavic?\), but the reconstruction of Proto-Slavic has changed significantly in the last years with the most vocal advocate for a more acurate reconstruction being Georg Holzer \(starting with Holzer 1995\). A good summary is given by Majer \(2020\). Calling this matter trivial is unexpected in a study which gives as one of its main objectives providing a tool for studying phonology.&#13;&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Holzer, Georg. 1995. Einheitlichkeit des Slavischen um 600 n. Chr. und ihr Zerfall. </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic">Wiener&#13;slavistisches Jahrbuch </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">41.55&#8211;89.</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.6pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;&#13;Majer, Marek \(2020\). Proto-Slavic. In Marc L. Greenberg \(ed.\), Encyclopedia of Slavic Languages and Linguistics Online. Brill. https://doi.org/10.1163/2589-6229_ESLO_COM_032015</span></p></body>) /Rect [ 252.769 590.471 430.515 606.855 ] /Subj (Hervorheben) /Subtype /Highlight /T (Anonymous) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
