1105 0 obj
<< /AP << /N 1579 0 R >> /C [ 1.0 0.819611 0.0 ] /CA 0.399994 /Contents <> /CreationDate (D:20260826205435+02'00') /F 4 /M (D:20260914175721+02'00') /NM (74454402-db58-4b75-a698-0f02fa0e538e) /P 35 0 R /Popup 1104 0 R /QuadPoints [ 90.0639 302.773 93.0639 302.773 90.0639 287.353 93.0639 287.353 ] /RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.2pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">It is worth noting that following Troubetzkoy \(1922\) the end of the Common Slavic period is commonly identified with the period of the yer shift.&#13;&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Trubetzkoy, Nikolay S. 1922. Essai sur la chronologie de certains faits phone&#769;tique du slave commun. </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic">Revue des E&#769; tudes slaves </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">2.217&#8211;234. </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:8.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">https://doi.org/10.3406/slave.1922.7258</span></p></body>) /Rect [ 89.5821 286.871 93.5458 303.255 ] /Subj (Hervorheben) /Subtype /Highlight /T (Anonymous) /Type /Annot >>
