<< /AP << /N 1589 0 R >> /C [ 1.0 0.819611 0.0 ] /CA 0.399994 /Contents (Perhaps the most extensive article on the \(alleged\) operation of the Progressive palatalization of *g is Vermeer \(2012\).\r\rVermeer, Willem. 2012. Why Baba-Yaga? Substratal phonetics and restoration of velars subject to the Progressive Palatalization in Russian/Belorussian and adjacent areas \(appr. 600\205900 CE\). In Riho Grünthal & Petri Kallio, A Linguistic Map of Prehistoric Northern Europe, 345\205370, Helsinki.  https://doi.org/10.33341/sus.1918.3241) /CreationDate (D:20260826222551+02'00') /F 4 /M (D:20260914175811+02'00') /NM (da920976-fcda-4163-9dd9-f248dd50288c) /P 35 0 R /Popup 1119 0 R /QuadPoints [ 206.729 68.709 209.229 68.709 206.729 55.8591 209.229 55.8591 ] /RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.6pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Perhaps the most extensive article on the \(alleged\) operation of the Progressive palatalization of *g is Vermeer \(2012\).&#13;&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-16.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Vermeer, Willem. 2012. Why </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-16.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic">Baba-Yaga</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-16.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">? Substratal phonetics and restoration of velars subject to the Progressive Palatalization in Russian/Belorussian and adjacent areas \(appr. 600&#8211;900 CE\). In Riho Gr&#252;nthal &amp; Petri Kallio, A Linguistic Map of Prehistoric Northern Europe, 345&#8211;370, Helsinki.  https://doi.org/10.33341/sus.1918.3241</span></p></body>) /Rect [ 206.328 55.4575 209.631 69.1105 ] /Subj (Hervorheben) /Subtype /Highlight /T (Anonymous) /Type /Annot >>
