1192 0 obj
<< /AP << /N 1631 0 R >> /C [ 1.0 0.819611 0.0 ] /CA 0.399994 /Contents (Here, another issue with this by many specialists considered outdated reconstruction of Common Slavic becomes apparent. The change *a > *o most probably occurred only after Liquid metathesis \(cf. Lindstedt's 1991 influential article\). Hence, the sequence *orC- most probably never existed in Proto-Slavic.\r\rLindstedt, Juoko. 1991. The Notational Fallacy in Common Slavonic Phonology, Scando\rSlavica 37, 108-122.) /CreationDate (D:20260826234055+02'00') /F 4 /M (D:20260914180030+02'00') /NM (b0cca37e-3c32-402b-860b-707811c49583) /P 37 0 R /Popup 1191 0 R /QuadPoints [ 199.744 633.873 231.736 633.873 199.744 618.453 231.736 618.453 ] /RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.6pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Here, another issue with this by many specialists considered outdated reconstruction of Common Slavic becomes apparent. The change *a &gt; *o most probably occurred only after Liquid metathesis \(cf. Lindstedt's </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">1991 </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.6pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">influential article\). Hence, the sequence *orC- most probably never existed in Proto-Slavic.&#13;&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-16.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Lindstedt, Juoko. 1991. The Notational Fallacy in Common Slavonic Phonology, Scando&#13;Slavica 37, 108-122.</span></p></body>) /Rect [ 199.262 617.971 232.218 634.355 ] /Subj (Hervorheben) /Subtype /Highlight /T (Anonymous) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
