<< /AP << /N 1633 0 R >> /C [ 0.588242 0.262741 0.988235 ] /CA 0.399994 /Contents <> /CreationDate (D:20260906162051+02'00') /F 4 /IT /HighlightNote /M (D:20260914180037+02'00') /NM (0896d320-5085-41eb-89d1-2609232b4b50) /P 37 0 R /Popup 1194 0 R /QuadPoints [ 341.63 620.073 477.613 620.073 341.63 604.653 477.613 604.653 56.8 606.273 211.287 606.273 56.8 590.853 211.287 590.853 ] /RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">In fact, the majority of researchers follow the reconstruction of the Moscow Accentological School and it is common practice to give accentological information in recent etymological dictionaries \(cf. those by Derksen, Snoj and Matasovic&#263; et al.\). I agree that it is still cumbersome to include this information, but I would rather state this as a reason and add that this information could be added in the future.</span></p></body>) /Rect [ 56.3181 590.371 478.095 620.555 ] /Subj (Kommentar zu Text) /Subtype /Highlight /T (Anonymous) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
