1281 0 obj
<< /AP << /N 1685 0 R >> /C [ 0.588242 0.262741 0.988235 ] /CA 0.399994 /Contents (I don't understand why this should be the case. If the argument is that a change affecting the entire Slavic speech area could not have been preceded by changes affecting only parts of it, it is contradicted by many changes in the history of Slavic.) /CreationDate (D:20260906180359+02'00') /F 4 /IT /HighlightNote /M (D:20260914180426+02'00') /NM (56d412a8-2c87-41bc-8825-bb7fcb9fed01) /P 40 0 R /Popup 1280 0 R /QuadPoints [ 485.052 744.373 503.712 744.373 485.052 728.953 503.712 728.953 56.8 730.573 528.133 730.573 56.8 715.153 528.133 715.153 ] /RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">I don't understand why this should be the case. If the argument is that a change affecting the entire Slavic speech area could not have been preceded by changes affecting only parts of it, it is contradicted by many changes in the history of Slavic.</span></p></body>) /Rect [ 56.3181 714.671 528.615 744.855 ] /Subj (Kommentar zu Text) /Subtype /Highlight /T (Anonymous) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
